 ## Key Design Decisions
 
 - **Commands over HTTPS, one authoritative board per event.** Editors submit commands to the server, which assigns each committed edit one event revision. Peer-to-peer or browser-side merging was rejected: the tenets require one authoritative revision regardless of delivery route, and offline editing is a non-goal.
+- **Self-hosted WebSockets for real-time delivery.** Committed changes are pushed to browsers via self-hosted WebSockets rather than HTTPS polling or a hosted realtime service. This avoids vendor coupling and recurring fees, accepts the operational burden of connection capacity and reconnect handling, and requires replayable revisions and reliable publication from the change store. See `docs/decisions/delivery-approach.md`.
